  "_commit": {
    "id": "bf6616552e125642ac04d795dec153c00ca63000",
    "author": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "committer": "tgirke <tgirke@citrus.ucr.edu>",
    "message": "Add runnable examples to the two hand-written man pages\n\ndownloadChemblDb.Rd and getUniprotIDs.Rd are among the 15 man pages\nwritten by hand rather than generated from roxygen, so the pass that\nadded runnable examples to the other pages never reached them.\n\ndownloadChemblDb() now shows where the download is cached and that a\nsmall sample of the same database ships with the package, which is what\nthe examples of the functions querying it use - so trying those needs no\ndownload. That also surfaces the \"this is a very large file\" warning\nthat was previously only an Rd comment, invisible to readers.\n\ngetUniprotIDs() shows the shape of its two result tables from the\nsnapshot already shipped in inst/extdata, which is useful on its own\ngiven the live UNIREF path depends on UniProt being reachable. The live\nquery stays under \\donttest.\n\nExported-object man pages with a runnable example: 57 of 64 (89%), up\nfrom 55. The threshold BiocCheck errors below is 80%, so this widens the\nmargin from three pages to five. The remaining seven are REST getters\nwith no local data to demonstrate on.\n",
    "time": 1792204583
  },
